    "narrative": "The LawDog starting lineup for 2026-06-12 is headlined by **Luis Arraez** (68.56) and **Taylor Ward** (67.28), who represent our most reliable assets today. **Luis Arraez** earns his high floor by leading off against Javier Assad, whose 4.63 xERA provides a favorable environment for **Luis Arraez** to maintain his batting average edge. Meanwhile, **Taylor Ward** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment, making him our strongest play despite the mediocre matchup against Canning. **Gavin Sheets** also captures that same park-driven upside, elevating his efficiency score to 64.98, while **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a core anchor (66.52) despite a tougher assignment against a 3.92 xERA arm like Flaherty.\n\nThe bench decision process was dictated by the league\u2019s premium on sprint speed and efficiency. **Bryson Stott** (48.48) was our most difficult omission; he was ultimately marginalized by Misiorowski\u2019s sub-3.00 xERA, which significantly suppressed his hitting ceiling compared to the active infielders. **Masyn Winn** (45.56) saw a boost from wind conditions but ultimately lacked the categorical necessity to crack a lineup where **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.52) holds a firm grip on the SS slot due to his matchup against the 4.33 xERA Lodolo. We continue to monitor the IL status of **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz**, as their absence remains a significant drain on our positional depth. No severe weather risks are currently flagged, but with **Jonathan Aranda** (58.51) facing a precarious platoon disadvantage against the lefty Aldegheri, we are keeping a close watch on his early-game at-bats to ensure he isn't pulled prematurely, which would hurt our category accumulation.",
